    "Scouting Notes": "POST DRAFT NOTES\n Saw his stuff jump this spring with fastball touching 95 with strong carrying traits, though the shapes get worse as the outings progress\n The fastball plays up due to huge extension (around 7 ft) down the mound \n Drop and drive mover, and the extension and loose arm action suggests he may ultimately live in the mid 90s and could flirt with the occasional radar gun reading up into the upper 90s. It's a good frame, good arm action and even better athlete.\n Spins the breaking ball north of 3000 rpm and shapes big benders in and out of the zone\n Upper 80s cutter that evaluators like more than area scouts do\n Low 80s changeup that should eventually turn into an average or better offering\n 17 on draft day, this is a pick that I think could look really, really good in a couple of years",
